Inka no longer decides by a content type's name. A template can be saved in any folder the site lets the user add the template's type to (that folder's @types), not only a Folder. The MCP server's new list_content_types tool gives the types a section takes, and create_page needs one of them rather than defaulting to Document. The markdown mount is told which types are folderish by its caller. Content deploy and the content validator find the site root where the export keeps it, not by a site called Plone. #663
